<title>USA: U.S. meat output 19.9 pct above a week ago - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. meat output 19.9 pct above a week ago - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Red meat production for week ending Saturday, July 12, 810.4 million lbs, up 19.9. - USDA</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING/1  BEEF   CALF/VEAL   PORK/2  LAMB/MUTTON  TOTALS/3</p>
<p>12-Jul-97     493.0	6.4	 306.7	 4.3	 810.4</p>
<p>05-Jul-97     417.3	5.5	 249.4	 3.9	 676.1</p>
<p>Change:	  18.1%    16.4%	 23.0%     10.3%	 19.9%</p>
<p>13-Jul-96     488.1	7.2	 296.4	 4.3	 796.0</p>
<p>Change:	   1.0%   -11.1%	  3.5%	0.0%	  1.8%</p>
<p>1997 YTD:   13127.1    170.6	8644.8     135.5     22078.0</p>
<p>1996 YTD:   13599.3    184.7	8885.6     142.9     22812.5</p>
<p>Change:	  -3.5%    -7.6%	 -2.7%     -5.2%	 -3.2%</p>
<p>			 LIVESTOCK SLAUGHTER (HEAD)</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING    CATTLE   CALVES/VEALERS	HOGS    SHEEP/LAMBS</p>
<p>12-Jul-97     705,000	   29,000     1,626,000	62,000</p>
<p>05-Jul-97     599,000	   25,000     1,322,000	56,000</p>
<p>Change:	  17.7%	    16.0%	   23.0%	 10.7%</p>
<p>13-Jul-96     700,000	   37,000     1,616,000	70,000</p>
<p>Change:	   0.7%	   -21.6%	    0.6%	-11.4%</p>
<p>1997 YTD:  18,988,000	  797,000    45,951,000   2,012,000</p>
<p>1996 YTD:* 19,390,000	  876,000    47,934,000   2,192,000</p>
<p>Change:	  -2.1%	    -9.1%	   -4.1%	 -8.2%</p>
